\name{cellucid_analysis_list}
\alias{cellucid_analysis_list}
\title{List the analyses}
\usage{
cellucid_analysis_list(viewer)
}
\arguments{
\item{viewer}{A viewer \code{\link{cellucid_view}()} or \code{\link{cellucid_serve}()} returned.}
}
\value{
A \code{cellucid_action_request}, at once and invisibly: the action is sent now, or when the viewer's channel opens.
\code{\link{cellucid_action_result}(request)} returns what it read: a list of \code{analyses}, \code{open} (The analysis open in the panel). Cells in it are original positions (0-based rows of the dataset's obs).
}
\description{
Each analysis of the panel and each analysis window: which is open, its pages, whether it has a result, is running, or is stale and why.
}
\details{
The viewer's action \code{analysis.list} (Analysis). It reads, and changes nothing: it makes no step of the history.
}
\seealso{
\code{\link{cellucid_act}()} sends any action by its type, and \code{\link{cellucid_action_result}()}
collects its answer.
}
\examples{
if (interactive() && requireNamespace("SeuratObject", quietly = TRUE)) {
  data("pbmc_small", package = "SeuratObject")
  viewer <- cellucid_view(SeuratObject::UpdateSeuratObject(pbmc_small))
  request <- cellucid_analysis_list(viewer)
  print(request)
  # cellucid_action_result(request) waits for what it read.
  cellucid_stop(viewer)
}
}
